&lt;b&gt;EORS_PPFS_II&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#x0D;
Exercise VO&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt; data and cardiac output data were collected from a Parvomedics True One &lt;sup&gt;™&lt;/sup&gt; metabolic gas analysis system.&#x0D;
&lt;P&gt;&#x0D;
&lt;b&gt;BEDREST_iRATS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#x0D;
The metabolic cost of exercise (MCE) was measured during select aerobic training sessions using a Parvomedics True One 2400 Metabolic Gas Analyzer.  Prior to the start of the exercise session, subjects were connected to the gas analysis system and breathed through a mouthpiece with their nose occluded or through a mask that coverd their mouth and nose so that all expired air could be measured.  Expired air was measured continuously for approximately 15 minutes prior to the start of exercise, throughout the exercise session, and post-exercise until oxygen consumption returns to near baseline levels (approximately 30 minutes).  The metabolic cost of the exercise session was calculated based on oxygen consumption above baseline measured during and post-exercise.  One MCE test was performed each week of bed rest.&#x0D;
&lt;p&gt;&#x0D;
Resting Metabolic Rate (RMR) was measured for 45 minutes using indirect calorimetry.  Following an overnight fast, light morning grooming, and vitals subjects were positioned supine in a dark or dimly lit and temperature controlled room.  The Parvomedics True One 2400 Metabolic Gas Analyzer (including skirted hood with laptop and calibration syringe) was placed over the subject’s head and chest area.  The hood was connected to tubing attached to the metabolic cart.  Expired air was continuously measured from which resting energy expenditure (kcal/min) could be calculated.  During the test, subjects were required to lay still and not sleep.  An Exercise Physiology test technician monitored the subject during the test.&#x0D;
&lt;P&gt;&#x0D;
&lt;b&gt;MR079G&lt;/B&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&#x0D;
Peak oxygen consumption (VO2) data were collected from a Parvomedics True One&amp;#0153: 2400 metabolic gas analysis system.  &#x0D;
